    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠσιόλογ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who inquires
				into natural causes and phenomena,</i> esp. of the pre-Socratic
			philosophers, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				986b14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				990a3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>de An.</u>
				426a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				641a7
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. μᾶλλον ἢ
			ποιητήν,</span> of Empedocles, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1447b19
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ φ.,</span> title of play by
			Sopater, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.101a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀρχαῖοι φ.,</span> title of
			work by Chrysippus, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.187
			</span></i>; as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρρησία
